@page "/"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Primitives
@inject PlaylistContentRepository ContentRepository
@inject PlaylistCacheLookup CacheLookup

<PageTitle>TheBluesland</PageTitle>
@* US-011 AC1: CanonicalPath is the fixed "/" - never the current request's own query string, which
   is what canonicalises every ?mood=/?genre=/?occasion=/?era= filtered view back to the base
   catalogue (spec 14) regardless of which filters are active on this particular request.

   2026-09-06: rewritten - the old "blues, rock and the records that connect them" copy dated from
   the original 8-15-playlist showcase, before the 2026-09-05 expansion to all 120 owned public
   playlists across sixteen genres (PlaylistTaxonomy.Genres); it undersold the actual catalogue. *@
<PageMetadata
    Title="TheBluesland"
    Description="TheBluesland is Mehmet's personal Spotify library - blues, rock, folk, electronic and everything between - each playlist introduced with a short curator note."
    CanonicalPath="/"
    ImagePath="/og-image.png"
    StructuredDataJson="@(new[] { WebSiteJsonLd })" />

<section class="brand-intro">
    <h1>TheBluesland</h1>
    <p>
        TheBluesland is Mehmet's personal Spotify library - blues and rock at its root, but grown
        to cover everything from folk to electronic - with every playlist introduced by a short
        curator note rather than left to speak for itself.
    </p>
</section>

@*
    US-009 design decision (still load-bearing under US-018's navbar restyle): filtering is a plain
    `<form method="get">` bound to [SupplyParameterFromQuery] array parameters below (@code block),
    evaluated server-side at static-SSR render time - not an `@rendermode InteractiveServer` island.
    The query string *is* the filter state (so opening a filtered URL directly reproduces the same
    result a form submission would), and a normal browser GET form submission both updates the URL
    and re-renders the filtered list with zero JavaScript/SignalR involved.

    US-018: the four dimensions are now `<details>`/`<summary>` disclosures instead of always-open
    `<fieldset>`s. `<details>` is native HTML - opening one reveals only its own panel (AC2) and
    needs no JavaScript (AC5), so the zero-JS guarantee above is unaffected. The active count in
    each summary (DimensionLabel) is the "Genre (2)"-style indicator from AC4.

    US-021: on narrow screens the same form additionally opens as a full-screen panel via the
    classic zero-JS "checkbox hack" - a visually-hidden `<input type="checkbox">` plus a `<label
    for="...">` that native HTML already toggles on click/tap/Enter with no JavaScript, styled with
    the `:checked` pseudo-class and the `~` general-sibling combinator in CSS.

    2026-09-06 fix: two real bugs found after shipping. (1) The four `<details class="filter-dropdown">`
    had no relationship to each other, so a visitor could open all four at once with nothing closing
    the others - a genuine UX mess (screenshot from production), not a rendering bug. Fixed with the
    native `name` attribute: same-named `<details>` form a browser-managed exclusive group (opening
    one closes the rest) - zero JS, zero CSS, a purpose-built platform feature for exactly this.
    (2) The mobile panel originally tried to force all four dropdowns' panels visible via CSS alone
    while their own `<details>` stayed closed - i.e. override a *closed* `<details>`'s native
    "don't render this content" behavior. That is the same category of bug that broke the outer
    wrapper before the checkbox-hack rewrite above: browsers do not reliably let author CSS override
    it, even when the CSS looks unconditional. `FilterDimensionOptions` (the checkbox loop for one
    dimension) is therefore rendered twice - once inside each real `<details>` for desktop, once
    inside a plain, always-rendered `.filter-mobile-dimension` block for the mobile panel - sharing
    identical name/value/checked attributes either way, so submitting from whichever copy is
    CSS-visible at the current breakpoint produces the same query string. Plain <div>s carry no
    "hide unless open" behavior of their own to fight, so this direction needed no override at all -
    only the safe, always-reliable direction (unconditionally hiding one whole copy or the other per
    breakpoint) is used anywhere here now.

    `body:has(.filter-mobile-toggle:checked)` locks background scroll (AC2) - if a browser lacks
    `:has()` the fixed, full-viewport panel still covers the list visually.
*@
<nav aria-label="Filters" class="filter-navbar">
    <input type="checkbox" id="filter-mobile-toggle" class="filter-mobile-toggle" />
    <label for="filter-mobile-toggle" class="filter-mobile-trigger">
        <span class="filter-mobile-trigger-label">@DimensionLabel("Filters", _criteria.ActiveCount)</span>
        <span class="filter-mobile-trigger-close">Close</span>
    </label>
    <form method="get" action="/" class="filter-navbar-form">
        <details class="filter-dropdown" name="filter-dropdown-group">
            <summary>@DimensionLabel("Mood", _criteria.Moods.Count)</summary>
            <div class="filter-dropdown-panel">
                <FilterDimensionOptions FieldName="mood" Values="PlaylistTaxonomy.Moods" Selected="_criteria.Moods" />
            </div>
        </details>
        <details class="filter-dropdown" name="filter-dropdown-group">
            <summary>@DimensionLabel("Genre", _criteria.Genres.Count)</summary>
            <div class="filter-dropdown-panel">
                <FilterDimensionOptions FieldName="genre" Values="PlaylistTaxonomy.Genres" Selected="_criteria.Genres" />
            </div>
        </details>
        <details class="filter-dropdown" name="filter-dropdown-group">
            <summary>@DimensionLabel("Occasion", _criteria.Occasions.Count)</summary>
            <div class="filter-dropdown-panel">
                <FilterDimensionOptions FieldName="occasion" Values="PlaylistTaxonomy.Occasions" Selected="_criteria.Occasions" />
            </div>
        </details>
        <details class="filter-dropdown" name="filter-dropdown-group">
            <summary>@DimensionLabel("Era", _criteria.Eras.Count)</summary>
            <div class="filter-dropdown-panel">
                <FilterDimensionOptions FieldName="era" Values="PlaylistTaxonomy.Eras" Selected="_criteria.Eras" />
            </div>
        </details>

        <div class="filter-mobile-dimension">
            <h3>@DimensionLabel("Mood", _criteria.Moods.Count)</h3>
            <FilterDimensionOptions FieldName="mood" Values="PlaylistTaxonomy.Moods" Selected="_criteria.Moods" />
        </div>
        <div class="filter-mobile-dimension">
            <h3>@DimensionLabel("Genre", _criteria.Genres.Count)</h3>
            <FilterDimensionOptions FieldName="genre" Values="PlaylistTaxonomy.Genres" Selected="_criteria.Genres" />
        </div>
        <div class="filter-mobile-dimension">
            <h3>@DimensionLabel("Occasion", _criteria.Occasions.Count)</h3>
            <FilterDimensionOptions FieldName="occasion" Values="PlaylistTaxonomy.Occasions" Selected="_criteria.Occasions" />
        </div>
        <div class="filter-mobile-dimension">
            <h3>@DimensionLabel("Era", _criteria.Eras.Count)</h3>
            <FilterDimensionOptions FieldName="era" Values="PlaylistTaxonomy.Eras" Selected="_criteria.Eras" />
        </div>

        <button type="submit" class="filter-apply">Apply filters</button>
        <a href="/" class="filter-clear">Clear filters</a>
    </form>
</nav>

<section class="catalogue">
    <h2>Playlists</h2>
    @if (_filteredPlaylists.Count == 0)
    {
        @if (_criteria.IsActive)
        {
            <p class="no-results">No playlists match the selected filters.</p>
            <a href="/" class="clear-filters">Clear filters</a>
        }
        else
        {
            <p>No playlists are published yet. Check back soon.</p>
        }
    }
    else
    {
        @foreach (var playlist in _visiblePlaylists)
        {
            <a href="@($"/playlists/{playlist.Slug}")" class="playlist-card-link">
                <PlaylistCard Content="playlist" CacheSnapshot="GetSnapshot(playlist)" />
            </a>
        }
        @* US-019 AC1/AC2/AC5: a plain GET link (no JavaScript needed) that cumulatively reveals
           the next PageSize playlists - the URL's own "page" value is the amount of content
           loaded, so a shared deep link restores exactly that much. wwwroot/js/infinite-scroll.js
           progressively enhances this into real scroll-triggered auto-loading; this link/markup
           is unchanged either way - it is the mechanism JS automates, not a fallback bolted on
           afterward. *@
        @if (PlaylistCataloguePage.HasMore(_filteredPlaylists, PageQuery))
        {
            <a href="@BuildLoadMoreUrl()" class="load-more">Show more playlists</a>
        }
    }
</section>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    private HttpContext? HttpContext { get; set; }

    // US-009 AC3: the query string is the entire filter state - no cascading interactive
    // component state, no client-side JS. Bound directly on the page per query-parameter name
    // (repeated "?mood=x&mood=y" is how a browser GET form submits multiple checked checkboxes
    // sharing one `name`, which is exactly how the OR-within-a-dimension selection above works).
    [Parameter]
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "mood")]
    public string[]? MoodQuery { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "genre")]
    public string[]? GenreQuery { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "occasion")]
    public string[]? OccasionQuery { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "era")]
    public string[]? EraQuery { get; set; }

    // US-019 AC5: the page number lives in the URL, not in any server/session/interactive state -
    // deliberately not carried as a hidden field on the filter-navbar form above, so submitting
    // that form (a plain GET that replaces the whole query string) naturally resets pagination
    // whenever the active filters change (AC4), with no extra reset code needed.
    [Parameter]
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "page")]
    public int? PageQuery { get; set; }

    private IReadOnlyList<PlaylistContent> _filteredPlaylists = [];
    private IReadOnlyList<PlaylistContent> _visiblePlaylists = [];
    private PlaylistFilterCriteria _criteria = PlaylistFilterCriteria.None;
    private IReadOnlyDictionary<string, PlaylistCacheSnapshot> _snapshots =
        new Dictionary<string, PlaylistCacheSnapshot>();

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        var cancellationToken = HttpContext?.RequestAborted ?? CancellationToken.None;

        _criteria = new PlaylistFilterCriteria(
            Moods: MoodQuery ?? [],
            Genres: GenreQuery ?? [],
            Occasions: OccasionQuery ?? [],
            Eras: EraQuery ?? []);

        // Already sorted by displayOrder, then publishedAt descending (US-009 AC1/FR-001).
        var allPublished = await ContentRepository.FindAllPublishedAsync(cancellationToken);
        _filteredPlaylists = PlaylistFilter.Apply(allPublished, _criteria);
        _visiblePlaylists = PlaylistCataloguePage.Take(_filteredPlaylists, PageQuery);

        // Never throws (spec 16.1): a DB outage must still yield a 200 with editorial content.
        // Only the playlists actually rendered on this page need a cache lookup.
        _snapshots = await CacheLookup.GetSnapshotsAsync(
            _visiblePlaylists.Select(playlist => playlist.SpotifyPlaylistId).ToList(),
            cancellationToken);
    }

    private PlaylistCacheSnapshot GetSnapshot(PlaylistContent playlist) =>
        _snapshots.GetValueOrDefault(playlist.SpotifyPlaylistId, PlaylistCacheSnapshot.Unavailable);

    private string BuildLoadMoreUrl()
    {
        var query = new Dictionary<string, StringValues>
        {
            ["page"] = PlaylistCataloguePage.NextPage(PageQuery).ToString(),
        };
        if (MoodQuery is { Length: > 0 })
        {
            query["mood"] = MoodQuery;
        }
        if (GenreQuery is { Length: > 0 })
        {
            query["genre"] = GenreQuery;
        }
        if (OccasionQuery is { Length: > 0 })
        {
            query["occasion"] = OccasionQuery;
        }
        if (EraQuery is { Length: > 0 })
        {
            query["era"] = EraQuery;
        }
        return QueryHelpers.AddQueryString("/", query);
    }

    // US-018 AC4: "Genre (2)" - the active-count indicator shown in each dropdown's <summary>.
    private static string DimensionLabel(string name, int activeCount) =>
        activeCount > 0 ? $"{name} ({activeCount})" : name;

    private string WebSiteJsonLd =>
        StructuredDataBuilder.BuildWebSite(BuildAbsoluteUrl("/"));

    private string BuildAbsoluteUrl(string path) =>
        HttpContext is null ? path : SiteUrl.BuildAbsolute(HttpContext, path);
}
